<p class="lt-chem-154799">What is the concentration of As(III) in a sample of water if its peak current is 1.37 &mu;A?</p>

<p class="lt-chem-154799"><strong>Solution</strong></p>

<p class="lt-chem-154799">Linear regression gives the calibration curve shown in Figure 11.4.18
, with an equation of</p>

<p class="lt-chem-154799">\[i_{p}=0.0176+3.01 \times[\mathrm{As}(\mathrm{III})] \nonumber\]</p>

<p class="lt-chem-154799">Substituting the sample&rsquo;s peak current into the regression equation gives the concentration of As(III) as 4.49 &mu;M.</p>
</section>

